  "primary_subject_agency_ids": [],
  "summary": "Brenham Police Department confirmed an internal affairs investigation into one of its officers after a watchdog group alleged on social media that the officer was terminated for misusing the department's Flock ALPR system. The city declined to confirm the officer's identity or the nature of the allegations, and a councilmember noted Brenham itself has no Flock contract \u2014 local Flock cameras are owned by Washington County, TxDOT, and private businesses.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "A social media post from a police watchdog group on Monday alleges an officer was investigated for misusing the department's Flock Safety automated license plate reader (ALPR) system, and that the investigation resulted in disciplinary action, including termination.",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "At this time, there has been no confirmation of Flock misuse at the Brenham Police Department.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "Soman told KBTX that while the city has access to other ALPR systems and technologies, the city doesn't have a contract with Flock. Soman said the Flock cameras in town are owned by Washington County, TxDOT and private businesses.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
  ],
